\title{Cubical sets and the topological topos}
\date{2016-10-17}
\taxon{Reference}
\meta{external}{https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.05270}
\meta{doi}{10.48550/arXiv.1610.05270}
\author{basspitters}

\subtree{
\taxon{Abstract}
\p{
[Coquand](thierrycoquand)'s cubical set model for homotopy type theory provides the
basis for a computational interpretation of the univalence axiom and some higher
inductive types, as implemented in the cubical proof assistant. This paper
contributes to the understanding of this model. We make three contributions:

\ol{
\li{
Johnstone's topological topos was created to present the geometric realization of
simplicial sets as a geometric morphism between toposes. Johnstone shows that
simplicial sets classify strict linear orders with disjoint endpoints and that
(classically) the unit interval is such an order. Here we show that it can also be a
target for cubical realization by showing that Coquand's cubical sets classify the
geometric theory of flat distributive lattices. As a side result, we obtain a
simplicial realization of a cubical set.
}
\li{
Using the internal `interval' in the topos of cubical sets, we construct a Moore path
model of identity types.
}
\li{
We construct a premodel structure internally in the cubical type theory and hence on
the fibrant objects in cubical sets.
}
}
}
}

